    "result_text": "All green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented email uniqueness for owner creation, rejecting with 409 when a lower-cased email already exists on another owner. Following the project's established telephone-uniqueness pattern, I added four small cohesive units rather than modifying any existing function:\n\n- **`RequireUniqueOwnerEmail`** \u2014 new step function. Runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (so the request email is already lower-cased), skips when email is absent (email is optional), and throws when any other owner's email matches case-insensitively.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException`** \u2014 checked exception (409-carrying message).\n- **`DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 maps the exception to a `409 CONFLICT` `ProblemDetails` response.\n- Wired a `uniqueEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `email` (normalize) and `unique` (telephone), under the existing `transaction` governance.\n\nStructural impact is minimal: no existing function bodies were changed (the wiring edit is in a YAML config, and each new class is a single trivial method with WMC_other = 0). The full test suite passes, including the new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test.",
